    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Role",
      "prov:value": "Extract the personas an instance's BPMN diagrams put in swimlanes as a\nSKOS concept scheme, and keep the retirement ledger that lets a dropped\nterm be told from an accident. Issue #596, bean `lqo9` slice 2.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean lqo9",
        "#596"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Role",
      "prov:value": "**Not the paper glossary.** `glossary-build` walks a\npaper's blocks and writes a LaTeX chapter from `defines[]`. This walks a\nknowledge graph and writes JSON-LD. Different corpus, different output,\ndifferent consumer — and there is a live ruling on whether they ever\nconverge, so do not merge them on your own initiative."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "A concept is a ROLE, not a lane name",
      "prov:value": "This is the rule most likely to be got wrong, because the issue's own\nwording (*\"a bpmn diagram swimlane has title/description\"*) points the\nother way."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A concept is a ROLE, not a lane name",
      "prov:value": "**Re-derive these before quoting them** — `bun run cat check:lane-documentation`\nfor the lane count, `bun run cat glossary:export` for the rest. They are a\n*dated observation*, not a property of the corpus, and this table has already\ngone stale twice: it read **157 task-containing lanes** measured 2026-09-21,\nand the check reported **182** on 2026-09-23 and **186** on 2026-09-24. Bean\n`lqo9` carries the same 157 and drifted with it, which is a bean and a skill\nagreeing and both being wrong — the case neither one can catch by being\ncompared with the other.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-09-23",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-09-23",
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`scopeNote` goes on the USAGE, never on the concept",
      "prov:value": "Of the 26 lane names appearing in more than one diagram, **26 of 26**\ncarry different documentation per occurrence — zero counter-examples.\nThat is the text doing its job. Hanging ten unattributed notes off one\nconcept asserts ten apparent contradictions about one word."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The ledger is the memory, and it is the only durable part",
      "prov:value": "The document is derived and rebuilt every run, so it has no memory:\ndelete a role and its concept simply stops appearing, which is what\n*\"never existed\"* also looks like. Retirement and accident must not look\nalike ([`deletion-requires-confirmation`](../../conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md)),\nso the one non-derivable fact — **this term was once minted** — is\ncommitted at `<instance>/glossary/glossary-ledger.json`, declared as\ngraph typology `swimlane-glossary` (`holds: \"state\"`; renamed from `glossary` on\n2026-09-23, when that name went to core's glossary kind; see\n`glossary-terms`, whose `glossary/` page reads this ledger as one source).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The ledger is the memory, and it is the only durable part",
      "prov:value": "**Usages are not ledgered**, deliberately: a usage is an occurrence,\nregenerated wholesale, while a concept is a term somebody may have cited.\nLedgering every occurrence — 157 when this was written, 186 today — buries\nthe records that matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Run it once per instance — never widen the scan",
      "prov:value": "`--instance <root>`, the shape `kg-export` and `translate-bpmn` already\nuse. Widening cat-harness's scan to reach bootstrap's diagrams\nre-introduces the leak `instance-graph-isolation.test.ts` exists to stop\n(`7u3g`), which two earlier sessions walked into.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 7u3g"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What it reports and never acts on",
      "prov:value": "- **Declared roles no swimlane draws.** They are still concepts —\n  omitting them would be `dh4f`, a glossary silently short of the\n  vocabulary it claims to index. The report says **which walk** found\n  nothing (\"no swimlane in `<instance>/` draws\") and splits the list:\n  a role a lane in ANOTHER instance binds (`partitionElementRef`) is named\n  with that diagram (`drawnElsewhere`), apart from roles no diagram in the\n  repository draws. Bean `nafz`: unsplit, a role drawn in\n  the content core read exactly like eleven drawn nowhere — a fact\n  about the walk phrased as a fact about the corpus. Reporting it is not\n  widening the scan: nothing outside the instance is bound or emitted.\n- **A lane binding naming a lane no diagram contains** (`fd6i`). Distinct\n  from a role whose lane exists but holds no task, which is not a defect.\n- **A lane whose binding is dangling, contradictory or unbound.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean nafz",
        "bean fd6i"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/swimlane-glossary.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What it reports and never acts on",
      "prov:value": "A lane declaring `<bootstrap.processes:role variable=\"true\"/>` is none of these. It\nemits a concept with a scope note and **no definition**, which is true —\nsee [`role-model`](role-model.md) and bean `ug4r`. `laneBinding()` is the\nonly route from a lane to a concept for exactly this reason: `variable`\nmust never be reachable as `unbound`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ug4r"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
